WEBVTT

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:02.530
Good morning!

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:05.120
I hope work's going well for everyone—

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:07.230
It's not.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.600
Oh, hello, Shimoda-kun.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:10.890
What's the matter?

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:12.350
It's always like this, no?

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:14.100
Is it, though?

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.380
Everybody's stuck right now.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:19.630
Unlike me, they got hit with 
some annoying requests.

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:21.290
Unlucky for them.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.130
Oh, there's an order from God for 
you personally, Venus-san.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.080
Order: Make horses fly somehow.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:40.180
Heaven's Design Team

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:06.220
"When you say horse, you think of Saturn-san,"

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:08.330
"but this time I specifically wanted 
Venus-san to have a go."

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:10.540
"That dragon from the other day was fun."

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:12.360
That's what God thinks.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.110
What, you're making a pegasus? I'm jealous.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:21.240
I'm sure it'll get done if everybody 
rallies behind you, Venus-san!

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.860
It won't be that easy.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:26.880
Saturn-san would be crucial, 
but he's busy right now.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:30.920
I have to work with Mars-san 
to repair the prototype lab.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.660
I need to do it because my 
grandson caused the damage.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:37.870
But I'm really looking forward 
to Ven-chan's pegasus, too!

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.250
I really don't like this.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:42.510
"Huddles in Corner" Type

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:44.290
Everybody's agonizing...

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.510
"Hugs Knees in Chair" Type

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.510
"Hides What He's Drawing" Type

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:48.760
Pluto-san seems to be relaxed.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.880
It may seem so, but she's the
 most stressed-out person here.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:55.370
I haven't heard back from 
the client in three days.

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:58.340
They said "ASAP," so I worked very hard.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.300
But I guess...

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.770
There was plenty of time.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.790
I can put some pressure on God!

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:05.820
It's fine.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:09.520
If you act like you're really enthusiastic,

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.790
it'll come back and punish 
you in the future.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.070
You know what I got?

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:17.460
"An animal that runs even 
though it has no legs."

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.920
To make it worse, I'm supposed 
to make three proposals.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:24.440
Lately, we only get orders 
that are like riddles.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.310
I want something sweet.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:30.050
I want a homemade caramel custard, 
where the caramel is slightly bitter.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:34.190
Why did you bring up such a 
specific treat just now?

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:34.190
<i>I had the impression that designers 
are always doing fancy work,</i>

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:36.180
<i>but I guess I was totally off!</i>

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.410
Venus-san, I got some additional input.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:42.700
He said: "You can do what you like!"

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:46.420
God must really trust your designs!

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:47.730
No!

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:50.890
That just means he'll leave it all to me 
and only give it some thought when it's done!

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:52.460
This is how you end up in Hell!

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:56.230
We already know what the problems are, 
so maybe I just need to go in headfirst.

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.470
S-So many muscles!

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:01.350
And so much horse poop!

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:08.850
<b>Pegasus
\h\h\h\h\h(Revised)</b>

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:06.110
I reduced the protein myostatin, 
which inhibits muscle growth.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:08.850
<b>M
y
o
s
t
a
t
i
n</b>

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.740
Isn't he so fit?

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:13.220
I'll just send this to God, then. And... send!

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:16.530
I can rest until we hear back, then.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:18.240
Oh, I already got a reply.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.740
Already?!

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.480
I'll just say what he said directly.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:25.570
What? I'm scared...

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:28.510
"That's not quite it," he says.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:29.360
What?

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:32.580
"I wanted something more surprising,
 not the same thing."

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:36.920
"Let your originality run wild, 
Venus-san!" End quote.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.620
See, there it is! 
The "I'll reconsider after seeing it" spiel!

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:43.270
Say what you want from the beginning!

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:45.790
I don't think shouting here will reach him.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:47.880
That's why I'm doing it!

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.400
How about this, then?!

00:04:54.520 --> 00:05:01.900
<b>Pegasus
Final
Revision</b>

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.640
Those are some cool lines.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:57.920
Exceptional!

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:01.900
I gave it less muscle mass 
to reduce its overall weight.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:04.740
It can't take off from the ground,

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:08.230
but if it jumps off a cliff and 
rides the air currents, it can fly.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:09.920
That's so original!

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:14.450
I sent it. I'm sure he'll like this one!

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:16.540
I hope so.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:19.910
Can I say it?

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:21.580
You already got a reply?

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.590
I already have a bad feeling, but go ahead.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:30.840
He says: "You don't have to stick 
to the horse part. Small is okay, too."

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:33.810
Why didn't he tell me that beforehand?!

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:37.460
I'll go and start from scratch...

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.520
G-Good luck.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.590
God, this is too much.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:46.390
Please be more understanding 
of the work the designers do.

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:48.120
Got it!

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.560
Thank you!

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:51.830
<b>2 Hours Later</b>

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:51.830
<b>Strawberry Shortcake</b>

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:57.320
I-I-I-It's done. Would you send 
it to the client, please?

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.700
Yes! Great work!

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:06.590
<b>Pegasus
Ultimate Final
Revision</b>

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:03.000
This is the ultimate final proposal 
for the revised pegasus!

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.760
What do you say about this?!

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:06.580
It's so pretty!

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.390
I worked off the image of a flower fairy.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:12.000
Since I made the arms into petal-like wings,

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.050
it can disguise itself as a flower.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:15.030
Wow.

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:18.230
For food, it drinks nectar. 
What do you think?

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:21.120
I like it! I'll send it now.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.530
May I say it?

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:30.670
Please.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:34.630
"The previous hellish iteration was better."

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:38.990
"Use a radial design, and don't make 
it colorful," he said.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.290
The previous iteration?

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:44.250
What's with the technical 
jargon all of the sudden?

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:48.220
I'm sorry! It's because I had 
to open my big mouth to God.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.250
I asked him to be more understanding 
of the work you designers do.

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:55.640
I thought he did that, but he's 
still just as unreasonable.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:07:00.290
It's fine. You said it because 
you wanted to help us, right?

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:03.100
The client's at fault here.

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:08.140
I can't think of anything.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:11.540
Ven-chan, can I see yours 
to take my mind off things?

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:12.910
Sure.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:14.730
We've all got it rough, huh?

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.590
So, go back to the previous 
iteration with the bony design,

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:22.170
make the face shorter, too,
and reduce the equine quality.

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:25.910
You know, while I'm at it, 
I'll get rid of the leg muscles.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:27.840
It's done!

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:33.680
<b>Pegasus Ultimate
Final Revision
Forever</b>

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:33.670
This is the ultimate final proposal 
for the revised pegasus, <i>Forever!</i>

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:38.580
Forever-chan hangs from high places,

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:40.680
then uses the momentum
 of its fall to take flight.

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:42.580
This way it can be light.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.690
That's so interesting!

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.940
So it spends its time hanging.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:52.440
Do you want to add the echolocation that 
dolphins have, so it won't bump into things?

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.450
<b>Dolphin Echolocation</b>

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.380
That's good! And for food...

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:58.210
From the way it looks, it should suck blood.

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:59.950
Nectar.

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:02.770
It would be cuter if it sucked blood.

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:04.810
N-Next time.

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:06.700
I'll send this off right away.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:10.090
God has spoken!

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.370
Accepted!

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:14.090
<b>Accepted</b>

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:14.090
<b>Greater
Horseshoe
Bat</b>

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.580
This is great! What a relief!

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:20.430
This is accepted, too!

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:22.550
What just made it?!

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:24.220
A running urchin...

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:31.240
<b>Lovenia
elongata</b>

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:31.240
<b>Accepted</b>

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.550
That's so freaking cool!

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:27.920
So fast! So awesome!

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:31.240
The thing I sent when I stopped caring passed...

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.100
Oh no, I forgot to delete that!

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:35.020
There are two sets of teats!

00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:37.900
Nothing will come out of the 
ones that are on top to us.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:40.630
The design already got accepted, though.

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:44.220
I'm done. Leave it.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:48.620
The other ones are... something the baby can 
latch onto so it won't fall down.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.130
<b>False Nipples</b>

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:50.330
"Something"?

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:53.130
<b>Latch</b>

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:57.550
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:56.880
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:00.550
What is better at flying? These or birds?

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:02.110
I think the bats.

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:04.770
Unlike birds, which use 
their entire arm to fly,

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:11.820
<b>Bat Wing</b>

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:11.820
<b>Thumb</b>

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:11.820
<b>Index Finger</b>

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:11.820
<b>Middle Finger</b>

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:11.820
<b>Ring Finger</b>

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:11.820
<b>Little Finger</b>

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:11.820
<b>Bird Wing</b>

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:07.600
bats spread their fingers to make a wing.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:10.410
Fingers allow for more fine-tuned control.

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:15.570
That just goes to show that the 
horse is the most supreme animal.

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:17.960
The horse has nothing to do with this!

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:21.540
...is what I'd like to say, but in 
reality, in terms of animal orders,

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.820
bats are close relatives of horses.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:27.130
There are bats that are 
basically horses. See?

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:30.420
That one's just got an elongated 
face to have a louder voice.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:33.060
Looking like a horse is just a coincidence.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:49.350
What's up with Venus? 
She's dressed to the nines.

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:51.200
She seems very enthusiastic.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:53.950
This time my order is for 
"a bird that's like a gem"!

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:57.170
You can't lift your mood
 if everything looks drab.

00:09:57.170 --> 00:09:59.810
Look at these opals. Aren't they gorgeous?!

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:03.700
What do you think about a bird that 
shimmers with rainbow colors like this?

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:06.630
If you keep being so confident—

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:11.100
Ah, yes? All right, understood.

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:15.960
You got a follow-up order. God would 
like to see "a bird that makes gems."

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:22.840
I did make birds feel attracted to 
shiny things, but making gems?

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:26.030
You can have one of these if you help me.

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:28.850
Keep them. I don't understand gems.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:33.970
That's right. This place is lacking 
in romance <i>and</i> romanticism.

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:37.300
What's that "opal" rock made of?

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:41.810
Opal is silicon dioxide. It's a mineral 
formed from silica dissolved in water.

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:46.370
Silica... Ah, like in those 
desiccants they put in cracker bags!

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:49.380
Don't say that! That's so unromantic!

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:54.410
Anyway, I made that rainbow-colored 
bird you asked me to make.

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:56.990
A bird that flashy will be easy prey.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:59.010
It'll be just fine!

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:03.880
It's so small it can land here,
weigh about this much,

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:05.990
and it's very fast.

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:09.160
So? You think it'll be attractive food?

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:10.240
I see.

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:13.410
Compared to the effort it takes to catch it,
 it's got too little nutritional value.

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:16.110
Exactly! So nothing to worry about!

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:17.770
Mars-san, let me see, please!

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:22.650
About that... I made it, but it 
doesn't have enough energy.

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:24.940
It's so small, it can't maintain 
its body temperature.

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:27.660
But I managed to make it sparkle!

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:29.170
Do you give up?

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:32.920
O-Of course not! I'll make it work somehow!

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:35.780
If it gets too cold, it should just eat.

00:11:35.780 --> 00:11:37.470
Something it can consume
 in large quantities,

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:39.580
is easy to digest, 
and is also high in calories.

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:50.430
Ah, nectar! That's romantic, 
and it's very nutritional.

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:53.700
But since I reduced its leg muscles,

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:56.630
it doesn't have the strength 
to walk along branches,

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:59.360
nor the power 
to tear apart the petals.

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:03.290
It's ephemeral and cute, 
but that's not enough!

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:06.320
Should I make it hover like a bee,
 and have it drink directly?

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:09.810
But then these traditional 
bird wings won't do.

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:12.840
I have no choice. I'll go 
ask the insect department.

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:14.790
Ow!

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:16.080
Venus-san!

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:19.610
That's what happens when you 
try to rush in shoes like those.

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:21.720
Putting on too many accessories 
is also dangerous.

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:25.930
That may be true, 
but don't deny me my looks.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:28.490
I'm not me if I don't look like this!

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:31.090
That's the same for the 
animals we're creating!

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:35.730
<b>Insect Department</b>

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:36.600
How does a bee fly, you ask?

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:51.250
<b>Bird</b>

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:51.250
<b>Up
and
Down</b>

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:51.240
<b>Bee</b>

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:42.900
The bee moves its wings back and forth, 
creating a vortex in the air that lets it fly.

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:51.240
<b>Back and Forth</b>

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:47.520
This design is more suited for hovering in midair,
rather than always moving forward.

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:51.260
I see. Since it's a small, light bird,
 it might be able to copy that.

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:54.500
If you include this ability, 
it won't just be able to hover!

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.220
It'll also be able to fly...

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:57.470
Backwards!

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:02.010
Yay, it flies!

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.250
It's able to drink the nectar, too!

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:09.490
Yeah, but since it needs to eat to live, 
I don't think it'll survive the night.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:10.540
If it falls asleep, it'll die.

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:11.650
If it sleeps, it'll die?!

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:14.570
Oh, right! What should we do?

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:16.510
Why not make it hibernate?

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:17.940
Just for the night,

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:21.030
make it lower its heart rate and 
body temperature, like during hibernation.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:25.530
That might let us slow its metabolism 
while sleeping to less than 10%.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:26.540
That'll work!

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:28.050
God has spoken!

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:30.030
Accepted!

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:36.040
<b>Accepted</b>

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:36.040
<b>Hummingbird</b>

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:36.040
Yay! The gem-like birdie is complete!

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:38.160
Thank you, Mercury!

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:40.910
But what exactly motivated you to help?

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:43.680
I take pride in my own style.

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:45.860
You're the same, right?

00:13:45.860 --> 00:13:48.300
It's only natural that 
I feel compelled to help.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:53.210
By the way, since you were struggling 
so much with that one,

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:54.690
I finished the other one.

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:59.530
Let me see... the bird that makes gems?

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:00.950
Will this work?

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:02.700
Yeah, that's simple.

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:06.420
Let me present it to you.

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:11.320
Doubling down on Venus's base setting 
that birds like shiny things,

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:14.260
this bird eats raw diamonds.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:17.120
Birds don't have teeth,

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:20.430
so they swallow pebbles to store in their gizzards,
 which are located in the back of the stomach.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:25.840
<b>Gizzard</b>

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:22.970
They use them to crush the food they eat.

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:25.840
S-So it's a diamond gizzard?

00:14:26.110 --> 00:14:29.330
But won't it not be able to fly 
if it eats rocks that big?

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:32.220
Exactly. That's why I made it flightless.

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:36.340
I made its legs stronger, so it can protect 
itself from enemies by kicking and dashing.

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:39.010
The raw diamonds it swallowed 
will tumble

00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:42.480
in the back of its stomach 
for years, eventually becoming

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:43.740
fully-polished gems.

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:45.970
These gems are made—

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:47.810
by this bird!

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:52.360
What is this?! It's looks 
scrawny and has no grace!

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:54.870
Why does this bird not have feathers?!
 That's not beautiful!

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:56.530
It doesn't need them, since it doesn't fly.

00:14:56.530 --> 00:14:57.960
That's so unromantic!

00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.490
Birdies need to be more like this.

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:02.000
Big eyes and eye lashes!

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.750
And luxurious feathers on the body!

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:04.510
Stop it!

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:06.580
You're ruining the beauty of its utility!

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:08.260
Let go!

00:15:10.070 --> 00:15:11.250
God has spoken!

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:13.510
Accepted!

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:15.680
<b>Accepted</b>

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.680
<b>Ostrich</b>

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.090
It's not beautiful.

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:19.670
It's inefficient.

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:22.140
That's not the design I wanted.

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:25.130
The client was happy, though.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.520
We did well.

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:30.780
You're right. The result was good.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.340
So, which gem do you want as a reward?

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:36.280
If there's someone you want to 
give it to, I'll help you pick.

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.490
The diamond will do.

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:44.030
I'll give it to Mars-san.

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:47.120
Wh-What? For me?

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:49.680
Are you sure?

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:50.800
Of course.

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:54.580
You were looking for a lens material 
with a high refractive index.

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:58.050
Thank you! This is a perfect lens
 to focus my laser beams.

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:02.560
This place is <i>severely</i> lacking in romance.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:07.820
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:06.800
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:12.130
Since these feathers shimmer because of 
the way light bounces off of them,

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:17.200
<b>Structural
Color</b>

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:14.380
this is called structural color.

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:15.720
Both soap bubbles...

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:18.950
...and the oil on ramen
 have structural colors!

00:16:19.260 --> 00:16:22.930
This has been a message from the insect department! 
We're experts on structural color.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:25.000
This is also structural color.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.600
When you tilt it, it shimmers 
with rainbow colors, right?

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:32.330
It's basically emitting color by 
stacking blocks that reflect light.

00:16:32.740 --> 00:16:36.350
Please look at this creature, 
which has mastered this technique!

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:48.450
Good morning, everyone—

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:49.350
Huh?

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:52.470
Oh, my!

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:57.620
Are you all part of an 
avant-garde art exhibition?

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:01.010
We're supposed to be playing hide-and-seek.

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:03.090
In clothes that stand out so much?

00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:05.780
Saturn-san, it's not possible...

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:07.200
Your striped horse thing, I mean.

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:08.760
No, wait.

00:17:10.950 --> 00:17:13.320
Even if an angel like Ueda-san can see us,

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:16.130
maybe animals won't be 
able to spot us so well.

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:19.680
It might be good camouflage against 
predators that crouch in the undergrowth

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:22.380
and attack their prey from there.

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:25.190
Shimoda-kun, crouch down there!

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:26.370
A-All right!

00:17:26.370 --> 00:17:28.800
Venus-kun, put these on.

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:32.400
Those are glasses that 
let you see like a lion.

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:35.670
How is it? Am I hidden?

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:37.420
You're highly visible.

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:39.700
Maybe we need to move around?

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:41.880
Somehow, you're even more visible.

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:44.650
It's like, do these guys 
not value their lives?

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:47.180
What are you all doing?

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:51.680
The client put in an order that said
 "make more stripey animals."

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:54.790
All right! Let's make a horse,
 a stripey horse!

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:57.530
That's why we're all thinking about it.

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:01.430
But we couldn't figure out any reasons 
to put stripes on a weak animal.

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:02.930
Here.

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:07.280
How about an animal that's
 cooled by the stripes?

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:12.620
When hit by the sun, the white parts and the 
black parts will have different temperatures.

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:16.820
<b>Warm air rises</b>

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:17.060
That will cause air to flow, 
which could help with cooling?

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:19.200
<b>Temperature difference
 causes air flow</b>

00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:19.200
Is that outfit making you cooler right now?

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:21.060
Not at all.

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:23.760
Could it be that Neptune-san hasn't slept?

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:27.240
He got an order from the client for
 "like a carnivore, but it's an herbivore."

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:28.320
He hasn't slept for two days now.

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:31.980
You don't have to force yourself 
to join this stripey business.

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:34.660
It's fine. It's a good distraction.

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:39.220
Maybe I should just make the animal 
I'm working on stripey, too.

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:40.600
That's it!

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:44.620
If I use the power of gut bacteria,

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:47.940
I can easily make a "carnivore" that 
can get nutrients from plants.

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:51.850
But since it won't have a lot 
of energy, it can't move very fast.

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:55.880
That's why I thought it should live in high 
altitudes where there are few enemies,

00:18:55.880 --> 00:18:57.820
but it snows there.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.950
It can't accumulate enough 
energy for hibernation...

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:04.030
Not to mention having enough reserves to 
grow in a winter coat fit for snow.

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:08.410
The way to resolve that is stripes,
or black-and-white!

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:14.210
<b>White for camouflage in the snow</b>

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:11.390
White for blending into the snow! 
Black for blending in during the summer!

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:13.790
<b>Black
for blending in during the summer</b>

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.840
<b>Panda</b>

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:14.070
In other words, a multi-season fur coat!

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:16.010
God has spoken!

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:18.220
Accepted!

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:23.390
<b>Accepted</b>

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:23.390
<b>Giant Panda</b>

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:23.380
I'm happy for you. It's cute 
how the eyes stand out.

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:27.740
Doesn't this also fulfill the 
"striped weak animal" order?

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:29.000
We're done.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:31.980
Chief, should we give up 
on the stripey horse?

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.150
Hm...

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:36.290
Here. I'm glad forgoing sleep paid off.

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:38.380
Thank you.

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:40.650
Send!

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:43.030
Neptune-san, you're amazing.

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.780
Oh, it wasn't so—

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:46.230
What is it?

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:49.220
No, it just looks like this boy's...

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:53.790
What's going on?

00:19:57.600 --> 00:20:01.260
Oh, no! Another design was stuck to it!

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:03.390
It was for the starfish!

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:04.420
Starfish?

00:20:04.690 --> 00:20:06.510
What are the characteristics of a starfish?!

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:07.750
It doesn't have a brain.

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:10.980
Instead, it has receptors 
on its feet for smelling,

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:13.320
and when it has detected prey, 
it moves toward that smell.

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:15.700
Incidentally, starfish are carnivores, too.

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:18.160
No! It's coming this way!

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:20.190
Ven-chan, you're scared so easily.

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:22.380
You're just touching it?!

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:23.830
It's fine.

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:29.120
It's multiplying?!

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:31.200
The base is a starfish, after all.

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:34.700
When you try to catch them, their hair 
comes out, and they multiply even more!

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:37.290
And they're scary!

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:40.750
This isn't good. We have to do something.

00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:44.300
It's because I didn't check properly.

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:45.520
No, it's because I didn't check!

00:20:45.520 --> 00:20:47.530
What are we going to do with these?!

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:49.760
It's all over!

00:20:50.860 --> 00:20:52.340
We're doomed!

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:54.560
You can relax!

00:20:56.090 --> 00:20:59.770
These are tsetse flies, 
which transmit sleeping sickness.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:21:01.280
<b>Tsetse Fly</b>

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.280
They sting areas that are uniform in color.

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:06.810
They should attack the pandas, since they 
have wider bands than your clothes.

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:08.380
Just stay put.

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:11.800
Stay put?

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:13.900
This is like a painting of Hell.

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:19.840
<b>They fell asleep</b>

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:27.090
For a moment, I had lost hope.

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:31.110
What a great idea to use tsetse flies.

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:34.500
Since we proved that it's less 
likely to be stung by flies,

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:36.360
can we give this horse a pass?

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:39.190
<i>That was great, but the horse again?</i>

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:41.100
God has spoken!

00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:43.340
Accepted!

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:45.360
<b>Accepted</b>

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:45.360
<b>Zebra</b>

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:45.360
Hooray!

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:48.820
I thought it wouldn't work 
on those mystery animals,

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:50.750
but they fell asleep quite easily.

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:53.130
Oh, that's because I cursed them.

00:21:53.390 --> 00:21:57.430
C-Cursed? Are angels allowed to do that?

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:00.170
Should I not have?

00:22:01.940 --> 00:22:03.870
Operational message!

00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:06.670
Ueda is going to Hell!

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:11.260
<b>Expelled</b>

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:46.530
<b>Next on the Agenda</b>
